# The loop counts down, so one of its copies asks the counter alone, and the front of that copy is entered out of turns of another: where it fails, the walk goes on at the entry of the closed copy, which believes
# what is known of `front`. That failing side is begun last. By then the start of a further copy that no turn had entered had jumped there with nothing known, the jump had taken what had met there, and the walk threw
# that away and began the block again with nothing. A Bun with assertions or ASan stopped; a release build struck the purchase and said nothing.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: 3,3 1,5,3
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(COUNT): compile WalkLoopsVersioned LoopVersioningAttemptsFailed mechanisms=all
# COUNT: statistic WalkLoopsVersioned 8
# COUNT: statistic LoopVersioningAttemptsFailed 0
